+## Why
+
+The current champion still makes unsafe final choices when a retrieved candidate
+contradicts an explicit tender requirement: ordinary ball-valve requests can
+select underground executions, and an electric actuator request can select an
+electric-ready execution.  These are selection failures rather than evidenced
+catalog-coverage or retrieval-miss problems, so a narrow, deterministic
+fail-open fallback is a higher-value experiment than another index change.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add deterministic recognition of a deliberately small set of literal,
+  selection-relevant tender requirements: ordinary ball-valve execution,
+  `under electric actuator` readiness, installed electric actuation, and
+  explicit full/reduced/standard bore wording.
+- After the reranker chooses a result, verify the selected candidate only
+  against those recognized requirements and its observable catalog data.
+- When the selected candidate conflicts and an already retrieved compatible
+  alternative exists, select the strongest compatible alternative using the
+  existing fused retrieval order.  Otherwise preserve the reranker outcome.
+- Expose enough result provenance to distinguish a retained reranker choice
+  from a compatibility fallback, and add focused tests for contradiction,
+  missing evidence, and no-compatible-alternative behavior.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `verifiable-selection-fallback`: Safely replaces a reranker-selected product
+  only when literal tender semantics and observable candidate evidence prove a
+  contradiction and an existing compatible candidate is available.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affected package code: `query_constraints.py`, `matcher.py`, and potentially
+  `models.py` for result provenance.
+- Affected tests: focused constraint and matcher tests using local fakes.
+- No prompt, catalog source, embedding model, Qdrant collection, BM25 corpus,
+  or index rebuild is required.

